## Non-negotiable

<!--
  Rules that hold regardless of how small the change looks. Keep this list
  short enough that breaking one is conspicuous. Four is a good number; ten
  means none of them are load-bearing.
-->

- {{TRUST_BOUNDARY_RULE}} — e.g. which inputs are untrusted, and what that requires.
- {{COVERAGE_RULE}} — e.g. new logic starts with a failing test; a bug fix reproduces first.
- {{TENANCY_OR_AUTHZ_RULE}} — e.g. every query touching scoped data carries its ownership predicate, and cross-boundary access needs an explicit regression test.
- **Completion gate:** not done until {{GATE_COMMANDS}} pass locally.

